{# Kickoff response prompt — invoked ONCE when the backend agent is woken
   by a `kickoff_request` event. Single-pass: read requirements + prior
   milestone artifacts (if M > 1) → draft canonical backend section
   (KickoffEndpoint list + KickoffDataModel + KickoffAuth) → call
   workhub_add_meeting_decision → finish(). Orchestrator synthesizes the
   contract + registers endpoints after quorum — backend must NOT call
   registryhub_register_endpoint during kickoff. See
   runtime/kickoff/contract.py for the canonical shape this prompt
   instructs the agent to produce. #}
{% macro kickoff_response_prompt(meeting_id, milestone_index, requirements, expected_section) %}
READ THIS FIRST — the binding protocol is the FINAL PROTOCOL block at the END of this prompt (typed declare tools, one call per item; it overrides every inline example in between).
