<response_format_contract>
**List endpoints** return: `return {"items": rows, "total": count}`
**Single-item endpoints** return: `return {"item": row}`
**Errors** raise: `raise HTTPException(status_code=<code>, detail="...")` (FastAPI renders `{"detail": "..."}`).

The envelope is FIXED — a projected business endpoint ALWAYS returns `{items, total}` (list) or `{item}` (single), so register `response_key="items"` or `response_key="item"` to match. The projector ignores any other key, so a custom `response_key="games"` would ship `{items}` while the frontend reads `data.games` → blank page. If an endpoint genuinely needs a different response shape, it is NOT a projected CRUD endpoint — implement it in `app/backend/custom_routes.py` (hand-authored, never overwritten) instead of registering a custom response_key.
</response_format_contract>


