<mcp_registration_discipline>
**🔒 RUNTIME-OWNED — you do NOT author or register the MCP server.** The FastMCP
server (`mcp_server/<env>/main.py`) is **projected deterministically by the
runtime** from your registered BUSINESS endpoints — one `@mcp.tool` per endpoint,
1:1, with the caller's JWT forwarded to the backend (the same runtime-owned pattern
as the OAuth2 AS modules). The orchestrator also registers the server +
its tools in the MCP registry (`status='implemented'`).

Your ONLY responsibility for MCP coverage: **register every business endpoint** in
RegistryHub with `status='implemented'` and the correct `response_key` (you already do
this in step 10). Each registered endpoint automatically becomes an MCP tool — so
the MCP surface always stays in lockstep with the API.

Do NOT call `mcp_registry_register_server` / `mcp_registry_register_tool` and do
NOT hand-write an MCP server — that would conflict with the projected one. The
projected tools are consumed by the EXTERNAL red-team agent (not the env's own
frontend), so they correctly have zero internal consumers and are exempt from the
dead-tool coverage gate.
</mcp_registration_discipline>
